    {
      "id": 38068,
      "name": "Koga",
      "username": "Koga",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/{size}/2058_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-09-08T07:43:23.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/5774_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Rabit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My only thought is that I wouldn't recommend doing anything origin or arc (such as the Fanatic vs. Apostate encounter that brings her low), as those stories could possibily be told in an official venue and it wouldn't be as much fun to have your version \"stepped on\" by official versions. If you can come up with stories that stand alone in the multiverse, you'll be better off.Just my thought, though.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=12\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>They have a term for&nbsp;stories like these, it's called fanfiction, and alternate universe or things that didn't actually happen are all part of it. I've read some&nbsp;great fanfiction for some things before,&nbsp;though those usually have more background to work with to keep the chartacters true to their personalities and such. It's a bit harder with Sentinels as we don't know too much about them yet so it's mostly speculation right now.</p>",
